<title>JAPAN: ALPINE SKIING-NATIONS CUP STANDINGS.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-NATIONS CUP STANDINGS.</headline>
<dateline>HAKUBA, Japan 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alpine skiing top five</p>
<p>womens Nations Cup standings on Friday:</p>
<p>  1. Germany	3,108  points</p>
<p>     (926 points downhill, 390 points slalom, 675 points giant</p>
<p>     slalom, 987 points super-G, 130 points combined)</p>
<p>  2. Austria	2,725 (787/792/599/487/60)</p>
<p>  3. Italy	  2,634 (559/650/895/490/40)</p>
<p>  4. Switzerland  2,037 (448/657/648/239/45)</p>
<p>  5. Sweden	 2,026 (232/880/425/389/100)</p>
<p>Top five overall Nations Cup standings:</p>
<p>  1. Austria	9,332 points (women 2,725 points, men 6,607</p>
<p>     points)</p>
<p>  2. Italy	  5,602 (2,634/2,968)</p>
<p>  3. Switzerland  4,742 (2,037/2,705)</p>
<p>  4. France	 4,017 (1,771/2,246)</p>
<p>  5. Germany	3,547 (3,108/439)</p>
</text>
